{"id":"33fad5560e7fe384","group":"58","path":"58/batch12/58-thm-loewenheim-skolem.md","title":"Löwenheim-Skolem Theorem","display":"thm-loewenheim-skolem — Löwenheim-Skolem Theorem","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-loewenheim-skolem","aliases":["58-thm-loewenheim-skolem","Löwenheim-Skolem Theorem","Downward LS Theorem"],"display":"thm-loewenheim-skolem — Löwenheim-Skolem Theorem","depends_on":["[[58-df-cardinal]]","[[58-df-elementary-substructure]]","[[58-df-satisfaction]]","[[58-df-cardinality]]","[[58-df-structure]]","[[58-df-infinite]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-loewenheim-skolem"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-loewenheim-skolem</span><span>Löwenheim-Skolem Theorem</span><span>Downward LS Theorem</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-loewenheim-skolem — Löwenheim-Skolem Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"5fb1c2241d1943d1\" href=\"?note=5fb1c2241d1943d1\" title=\"58-df-cardinal\">58-df-cardinal</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"faf104362ffe13b3\" href=\"?note=faf104362ffe13b3\" title=\"58-df-elementary-substructure\">58-df-elementary-substructure</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"8b6a90316aad78a4\" href=\"?note=8b6a90316aad78a4\" title=\"58-df-satisfaction\">58-df-satisfaction</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"2be08d4ee8aa1590\" href=\"?note=2be08d4ee8aa1590\" title=\"58-df-cardinality\">58-df-cardinality</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"d9b8711cda3f31ca\" href=\"?note=d9b8711cda3f31ca\" title=\"58-df-structure\">58-df-structure</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"be9675f035d2c1e2\" href=\"?note=be9675f035d2c1e2\" title=\"58-df-infinite\">58-df-infinite</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal{M}\">\\(\\mathcal{M}\\)</span> (<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L\">\\(L\\)</span>-structure, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"d9b8711cda3f31ca\" href=\"?note=d9b8711cda3f31ca\" title=\"58-df-structure\">58-df-structure</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A \\subseteq \\mathrm{Univ}(\\mathcal M)\">\\(A \\subseteq \\mathrm{Univ}(\\mathcal M)\\)</span> (parameter set)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa,\\lambda\">\\(\\kappa,\\lambda\\)</span> (cardinals controlling the size of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal{M}\">\\(\\mathcal{M}\\)</span> and of the elementary submodel, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"2be08d4ee8aa1590\" href=\"?note=2be08d4ee8aa1590\" title=\"58-df-cardinality\">58-df-cardinality</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S\\)</span> (cardinal predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-9\" data-note=\"5fb1c2241d1943d1\" href=\"?note=5fb1c2241d1943d1\" title=\"58-df-cardinal\">58-df-cardinal</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Infinite}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Infinite}_S\\)</span> (infinite-cardinal predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-10\" data-note=\"be9675f035d2c1e2\" href=\"?note=be9675f035d2c1e2\" title=\"58-df-infinite\">58-df-infinite</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Struct}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Struct}_S\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Univ}\">\\(\\mathrm{Univ}\\)</span> (structure predicate and universe operator, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-11\" data-note=\"d9b8711cda3f31ca\" href=\"?note=d9b8711cda3f31ca\" title=\"58-df-structure\">58-df-structure</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ElementarySubstructure}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ElementarySubstructure}_S\\)</span> (elementary-substructure predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-12\" data-note=\"faf104362ffe13b3\" href=\"?note=faf104362ffe13b3\" title=\"58-df-elementary-substructure\">58-df-elementary-substructure</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}loewenheim\\text{-}skolem} \\vdash \\mathrm{Struct}_S(\\mathcal{M},L)\\land \\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\land\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(\\lambda)\\land |\\mathrm{Univ}(\\mathcal M)|=\\kappa\\land \\mathrm{Infinite}_S(\\lambda)\\land \\exists R,F,C,a\\;\\bigl(L=\\langle R,F,C,a\\rangle\\land|R\\cup F\\cup C|\\leq\\lambda\\bigr)\\land A\\subseteq\\mathrm{Univ}(\\mathcal M)\\land |A|\\leq\\lambda\\leq\\kappa\\to\\exists\\mathcal N\\in V\\;(\\mathrm{ElementarySubstructure}_S(\\mathcal N,\\mathcal M,L)\\land A\\subseteq\\mathrm{Univ}(\\mathcal N)\\land|\\mathrm{Univ}(\\mathcal N)|=\\lambda)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}loewenheim\\text{-}skolem} \\vdash \\mathrm{Struct}_S(\\mathcal{M},L)\\land \\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\land\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(\\lambda)\\land |\\mathrm{Univ}(\\mathcal M)|=\\kappa\\land \\mathrm{Infinite}_S(\\lambda)\\land \\exists R,F,C,a\\;\\bigl(L=\\langle R,F,C,a\\rangle\\land|R\\cup F\\cup C|\\leq\\lambda\\bigr)\\land A\\subseteq\\mathrm{Univ}(\\mathcal M)\\land |A|\\leq\\lambda\\leq\\kappa\\to\\exists\\mathcal N\\in V\\;(\\mathrm{ElementarySubstructure}_S(\\mathcal N,\\mathcal M,L)\\land A\\subseteq\\mathrm{Univ}(\\mathcal N)\\land|\\mathrm{Univ}(\\mathcal N)|=\\lambda)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Löwenheim (1915), Skolem (1920): fundamental model theory theorem.</li>\n<li>&quot;Skolem paradox&quot;: countable model of ZFC exists (even though ZFC says there are uncountable sets).</li>\n<li>Countable model of ZFC: the &quot;uncountable&quot; sets inside are externally countable.</li>\n<li>There is also an upward form producing elementary extensions of arbitrarily large cardinality.</li>\n<li>For countable languages, every infinite model has a countable elementary submodel.</li>\n<li>Foundation for: forcing, Skolem hulls, elementary chains.</li>\n<li>Used in: consistency proofs, independence proofs.</li>\n<li>The conclusion uses the dependency's exact argument order: substructure, ambient structure, then language.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-cardinal","status":"resolved","id":"5fb1c2241d1943d1","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-cardinal]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-elementary-substructure","status":"resolved","id":"faf104362ffe13b3","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-elementary-substructure]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-satisfaction","status":"resolved","id":"8b6a90316aad78a4","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-satisfaction]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-cardinality","status":"resolved","id":"2be08d4ee8aa1590","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-cardinality]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-structure","status":"resolved","id":"d9b8711cda3f31ca","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-structure]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-infinite","status":"resolved","id":"be9675f035d2c1e2","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-infinite]]","embed":false},{